[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955658116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116738#issuecomment-3955658116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116738","id":3955658116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rxo2E","user":{"login":"ScatteredComet","id":120208759,"node_id":"U_kgDOByo9dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120208759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet","html_url":"https://github.com/ScatteredComet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-25T00:46:33Z","updated_at":"2026-02-25T00:50:50Z","body":"Are you saying you want to be able to view the scene from the scene's camera? If so that's already a feature.\n\nIf you want to preview the scene (with correct billboarding) you can click on the camera3D and tick the preview option that appears in the editor window. Then scene will be rendered from the selected camera. That way theres no need to guesstimate the camera transform.\n\n<img width=\"416\" height=\"106\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/192f6aa7-482d-44c6-ba7e-d9f2c5cc29ae\" />\n\nMaybe you're after something else; feel free to expand more on what you're looking for if I've misunderstood.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3955658116/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964469204","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116738#issuecomment-3964469204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116738","id":3964469204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sTP_U","user":{"login":"louiidev","id":12892064,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODkyMDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12892064?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev","html_url":"https://github.com/louiidev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/louiidev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T06:43:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T06:43:32Z","body":"> esstimate the camera transform.\n\nThanks, yeah, I’m aware of the camera preview option.\n\nThe issue for me is that when using the preview, you lose some of the normal editor workflow conveniences (like comfortably using gizmos and interacting with the scene the way you usually would). It makes iteration feel a bit awkward.\n\nWhat feels unintuitive to me is that the billboarded `Sprite3D` faces the editor camera rather than the scene’s `Camera3D`. I understand there may be architectural reasons for this, but from a scene-authoring perspective it makes it harder to visualize how the scene will actually look at runtime.\n\nMaybe this is by design, but it does feel slightly at odds with how you'd expect billboarding to behave in the context of a scene that already has a defined camera.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964469204/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993275490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116738#issuecomment-3993275490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116738","id":3993275490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uBIxi","user":{"login":"ScatteredComet","id":120208759,"node_id":"U_kgDOByo9dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/120208759?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet","html_url":"https://github.com/ScatteredComet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ScatteredComet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T20:11:48Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T20:12:22Z","body":"As a workaround, you could make a tool script which points a sprite3D towards a given camera3D (using the [`look_at()` function](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_node3d.html#class-node3d-method-look-at)). Then turn billboarding on in the sprite3D's ready function. I think that would act how you're describing?\n\nIMO the main point of billboarding is to be the cheapest rendering option possible, and I think this is pretty easy to workaround. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993275490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993287661","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116738#issuecomment-3993287661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116738","id":3993287661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uBLvt","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T20:14:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T20:14:12Z","body":"I don't think it is possible to do this without major changes to the rendering system, billboard sprites are handled inside the rendering system, not with code, so how would the shader know what the camera you want is doing?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3993287661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]